---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const limits = [
  { title: 'Research prototype', detail: 'This is a proof of concept. It is not a certified medical device: further testing and validation would be needed, and every mechanism still has to be developed in medical-grade silicone.' },
  { title: 'Parabolic flight testing', detail: `The parabolic flights were, to our knowledge, the first time menstrual management was tested in a reduced gravity context, but each parabola lasted only about ${site.flight.reduced_gravity_s} s. Representing an astronaut wearing such a device calls for longer campaigns, which would also let the tampon (the reference device) and the SpaceCups collect more fluid in flight.` },
  { title: 'Experimental set-up', detail: 'In flight the SpaceCups and tampons were inserted into a model vagina that does not accurately represent the female anatomy. It was also too opaque to track the behaviour of the menstrual blood adequately.' },
];
---
<section id="limits">
  <h2>Limitations</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    The tests show that the Flower mechanism can be inserted, closed and
    removed during short periods of reduced gravity. They do not yet
    establish how well it contains fluid over long-duration use.
  </p>

  <ul class="limits-list">
    {limits.map((l) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{l.title}</strong>
        <span>{l.detail}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</section>

<style>
  .limits-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .limits-list li {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--ghe-red);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .limits-list strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .limits-list span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
